    <code class="f-rule">core-seo/title-length</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No title to measure</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Rewrite the title to sit between 30 and 60 characters so it is not truncated in search results.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="core-seo">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Meta description length</p>
    <code class="f-rule">core-seo/meta-description-length</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No description to measure</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Trim or expand the meta description to 70 to 160 characters.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="core-seo">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">H1 length</p>
    <code class="f-rule">core-seo/h1-length</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">H1 is short (9 chars)</p>
  
  <pre dir="auto"><code>Not found</code></pre>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Rewrite the H1 to sit between 10 and 70 characters. One word says nothing; a sentence is not a heading.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="core-seo">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Canonical URL present</p>
    <code class="f-rule">core-seo/canonical-present</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No canonical link</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add &#60;link rel=&#34;canonical&#34; href=&#34;...&#34;&#62; pointing to the preferred absolute URL of this page.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="core-seo">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Charset declared</p>
    <code class="f-rule">core-seo/charset-declared</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No charset declared</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add &#60;meta charset=&#34;utf-8&#34;&#62; as the first tag in &#60;head&#62;.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="core-seo">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Open Graph basics</p>
    <code class="f-rule">core-seo/open-graph-basics</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Missing Open Graph tags: og:title, og:description, og:image</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add og:title, og:description, and og:image meta tags so the page previews well when shared.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="content">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Word count</p>
    <code class="f-rule">content/word-count</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Thin content (2 words)</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add more substantive content. Thin pages rank poorly. Aim for at least 300 meaningful words.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="content">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">HTML lang attribute</p>
    <code class="f-rule">content/html-lang</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Missing lang on &#60;html&#62;</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Set the language on the root element, e.g. &#60;html lang=&#34;en&#34;&#62;.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="structured-data">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Organization or WebSite schema</p>
    <code class="f-rule">structured-data/org-or-website</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No Organization or WebSite schema</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add Organization or WebSite JSON-LD so search engines understand the site entity and can show a knowledge panel.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="structured-data">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">JSON-LD present</p>
    <code class="f-rule">structured-data/jsonld-present</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No JSON-LD structured data</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add JSON-LD structured data describing the page, e.g. Article, Product, or Organization.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="security">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">HSTS header</p>
    <code class="f-rule">security/hsts</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Missing Strict-Transport-Security</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add the Strict-Transport-Security header to enforce HTTPS on future visits.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="security">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Content-Security-Policy</p>
    <code class="f-rule">security/csp</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Missing Content-Security-Policy</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add a Content-Security-Policy header to limit what scripts and resources can load.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="security">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Clickjacking protection</p>
    <code class="f-rule">security/x-frame-options</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No X-Frame-Options or frame-ancestors</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Set X-Frame-Options: DENY or a CSP frame-ancestors directive to block clickjacking.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="security">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">X-Content-Type-Options</p>
    <code class="f-rule">security/x-content-type-options</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Missing X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff to stop MIME-type sniffing.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="security">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Referrer-Policy</p>
    <code class="f-rule">security/referrer-policy</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Missing Referrer-Policy</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add a Referrer-Policy header, e.g. strict-origin-when-cross-origin.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="crawlability">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Canonical valid</p>
    <code class="f-rule">crawlability/canonical-valid</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No canonical to validate</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Use an absolute, valid URL in the canonical link.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="social-media">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Twitter Card</p>
    <code class="f-rule">social-media/twitter-card</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No twitter:card meta</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add &#60;meta name=&#34;twitter:card&#34; content=&#34;summary_large_image&#34;&#62; so links preview well on X/Twitter.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="social-media">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Open Graph image is absolute</p>
    <code class="f-rule">social-media/og-image-absolute</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No og:image to validate</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>og:image must be an absolute https URL. Social platforms cannot resolve relative paths.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="legal">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Privacy policy link</p>
    <code class="f-rule">legal/privacy-policy</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No privacy policy link found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Link to a privacy policy. Most jurisdictions require one if you collect any personal data.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="analytics">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Analytics installed</p>
    <code class="f-rule">analytics/tag-present</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No analytics tag detected</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Install an analytics tag (GA4, Plausible, Fathom, etc.) so you can measure traffic and behaviour.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="eeat">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Author attribution</p>
    <code class="f-rule">eeat/author</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No author attribution found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Attribute content to a named author via a byline, rel=author, or schema author property.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="performance">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Text compression</p>
    <code class="f-rule">performance/text-compression</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">HTML response is not compressed</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Enable gzip or Brotli compression on HTML, CSS, and JS responses to cut transfer size.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="performance">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Cache headers</p>
    <code class="f-rule">performance/cache-control</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No Cache-Control header</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Send a Cache-Control header so browsers and CDNs can cache responses.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="performance">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge warn"
      ><span class="mark"></span>WARN</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">HTTP/2 or HTTP/3</p>
    <code class="f-rule">performance/http-version</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">Served over HTTP/1.1</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Serve the site over HTTP/2 or HTTP/3. Most hosts and CDNs turn it on with one setting.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="structured-data">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Breadcrumb schema</p>
    <code class="f-rule">structured-data/breadcrumb-valid</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No breadcrumb schema</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add BreadcrumbList structured data to show the page&#39;s position in the site.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="structured-data">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">FAQPage schema</p>
    <code class="f-rule">structured-data/faqpage-valid</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No FAQPage schema</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Give FAQPage a mainEntity list of Question items, each with a name and an acceptedAnswer holding the answer text.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="structured-data">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">HowTo schema</p>
    <code class="f-rule">structured-data/howto-valid</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No HowTo schema</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Give HowTo a name and a step list of HowToStep items (or HowToSection items holding them), each with text.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="security">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy</p>
    <code class="f-rule">security/coop</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy header</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin to isolate your browsing context.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="security">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Permissions-Policy</p>
    <code class="f-rule">security/permissions-policy</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No Permissions-Policy header</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add a Permissions-Policy header to restrict powerful browser features the site does not use.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="social-media">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Social profile links</p>
    <code class="f-rule">social-media/profile-links</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No social profile links found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Link to your social profiles so visitors and search engines can connect your brand accounts.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="internationalization">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">hreflang annotations</p>
    <code class="f-rule">internationalization/hreflang-present</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No hreflang alternates (fine for a single-language site)</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>If the site serves more than one language or region, add hreflang link alternates so Google serves the right version.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="legal">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Terms of service link</p>
    <code class="f-rule">legal/terms</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No terms of service link found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Link to terms of service or terms and conditions to set the rules for using your site.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="legal">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Cookie consent</p>
    <code class="f-rule">legal/cookie-consent</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No cookie consent banner detected</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>If you set non-essential cookies, show a consent banner (a CMP) to comply with privacy law.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="legal">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Contact information</p>
    <code class="f-rule">legal/contact</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No contact link found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Provide a contact link or page. It builds trust and is a positive E-E-A-T signal.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="legal">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Refund or returns page</p>
    <code class="f-rule">legal/refund-policy</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No refund or returns page link found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>If you sell anything, link to a refund or returns policy from every page, usually in the footer.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="legal">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Ads or affiliate disclosure</p>
    <code class="f-rule">legal/ad-disclosure</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No affiliate links or ads detected</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Pages with affiliate links or ads should say so near the top, for example &#34;This post contains affiliate links&#34;.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="eeat">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Published or updated date</p>
    <code class="f-rule">eeat/date</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No published or updated date found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Show a published or last-updated date. Freshness and transparency are trust signals.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="eeat">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Outbound citations</p>
    <code class="f-rule">eeat/outbound-citations</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No outbound citations</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Cite authoritative external sources. Outbound links to reputable sites support your claims.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="eeat">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">About page</p>
    <code class="f-rule">eeat/about-page</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No about page link found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Link to an about page that explains who is behind the site. It is a core trust signal.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="eeat">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Phone number and address</p>
    <code class="f-rule">eeat/contact-details</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No phone number or address on the page</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Show a phone number and a physical address, in the footer or on a contact page linked from every page.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="eeat">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Editorial policy</p>
    <code class="f-rule">eeat/editorial-policy</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No editorial policy link found</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Publish an editorial policy (how you research, review and correct content) and link to it.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="eeat">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">NAP consistency</p>
    <code class="f-rule">eeat/nap-consistency</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No LocalBusiness schema</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Show the same business name, address and phone in the page text as in the LocalBusiness schema.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="performance">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Font loading</p>
    <code class="f-rule">performance/font-display</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No web fonts declared in the HTML (external stylesheets are not read)</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Set font-display: swap (or optional) on every @font-face, and add &#38;display=swap to Google Fonts links, so text shows while fonts load.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="performance">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Resource hints for third-party origins</p>
    <code class="f-rule">performance/resource-hints</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No third-party origins for scripts, styles or fonts</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Add &#60;link rel=&#34;preconnect&#34;&#62; (or dns-prefetch) for each third-party origin the page loads scripts, styles or fonts from.</span>
  </p>
  
</li><li class="finding" data-cat="performance">
  <div class="f-head">
    <span class="badge info"
      ><span class="mark"></span>INFO</span
    >
    <p class="f-title">Third-party scripts</p>
    <code class="f-rule">performance/third-party-scripts</code>
  </div>
  <p class="f-msg" dir="auto">No third-party scripts</p>
    
  <p class="f-fix">
    <span class="f-fix-label">Fix</span> <span>Drop third-party scripts you do not need, and load the rest with async or defer.</span>
  </p>
  
</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="panel pm">
             
